# <type>(<scope>): <subject> (72 characters) which is here             #

# Leave the next line blank

# Body - the *why*. For refactors, which boundary was wrong. For
# services, what broke or what the old setting cost you.
# Wrap at 72 chars. ################################## which is here:  #

# The following fields are optional. Fill them out if they apply.
# Rebuilt-on:   hosts actually switched onto this commit before pushing
# Breaking:     manual steps needed on rebuild (state migration, rekey)
# Refs:

# ----- END COMMIT MESSAGE -----
#
# <type> is one of:
#   feat      New capability - a new aspect, service, host, or user
#   fix       Something was broken - eval failure, wrong port, dead
#             service, a setting that did not do what it claimed
#   tune      Settings change on something that already works -
#             keybinds, theme, package set, retention windows
#   refactor  Restructure the module tree; evaluated config unchanged
#   flake     Input bumps and lockfile changes
#   secrets   agenix - new .age files, rekeying, recipient changes
#   docs      CLAUDE.md, README, regenerated aspect index
#   chore     Repo maintenance - justfile, gitignore, formatter,
#             inventory
#
# <scope> is optional. Pick the first that applies:
#   1. the aspect name       wireguard, caddy, neovim, plasma
#   2. the host              hades, odysseus, tantalus, ubuntu
#   3. the tree area         profiles, system, home, inventory
#   4. omit it               the change is genuinely repo-wide
#
# <subject> is imperative mood, as if "This commit will..." is
# prepended. Do not capitalize, and omit the full stop.
#
# Examples:
#   feat(wireguard): add wireguard aspect
#   feat(hades): import wireguard aspect
#   feat(tantalus): add self-hosted gitlab instance
#   fix(caddy): stop freshrss vhost from stealing :443
#   fix(tex): stop eager `mat` -> matrix substitution
#   tune(plasma): rebind emoji selector to meta+.
#   tune(neovim): add markdown preview
#   refactor(profiles): split gui apps out of core
#   refactor: hoist libreoffice into system-desktop
#   flake: bump nixpkgs and home-manager
#   secrets(freshrss): rekey for tantalus host key
#   docs: regenerate aspect index
#   chore(inventory): add hades to machines.toml
#
# Three exceptions to the subject line rules:
#   1. "Initial commit"     for the first commit in a repository
#   2. "Merge branch..."    the default message for automatic merges
#   3. "Revert..."          the default message for reverting commits
